954, child tablet registration to the sys catalog is atomic. If the sys catalog has `split_tablet_ids` entries, it is guaranteed to include both the split children and not just one of them. Therefore there is no need to regenerate and register new child tablets. Hence we can remove any logic to create and register child tablets from this code path.\n\nThis refactor helps argue correctness better if we move to N-way splits. The logic to fill holes in the child tablet array for an N-way split may not be trivial.\n\n### Issue Type\n\nkind/enhancement\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [x] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-19462]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-19462?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/29643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/29643/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]